@startuml target_follow_up_handoff
' Target-only. Direction accepted; disabled in the current product.
' Source: pi-mono-java@dfb90cac4e233e09a0b8f047f7e9f4682f5ad238
' campusclaw/src/main/java/com/huawei/hicampus/claw/codingagent/runtimeapi/session/RuntimeSessionControlService.java
' Symbols: acceptLocked, requireRunningHolder, queueControl. Observed behavior: local Holder queues.
' Source: pi-mono@5cd93f688aaab89dbb6dfa4aca535f21796ae185
' packages/agent/src/agent-loop.ts: runLoop. Observed behavior: follow-up continues the same loop.
' Design reason: durable application handoff avoids sticky routing and live output relay.
autonumber
hide footbox
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam maxMessageSize 190
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #475569
  LifeLineBorderColor #94A3B8
  ParticipantBorderColor #64748B
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  GroupBorderColor #94A3B8
  GroupBackgroundColor #F1F5F9
}
title Future FollowUp: Cross-instance Handoff (Disabled)
actor "Caller via Mate" as C
participant "Instance A\nM1 execution" as A
participant "Instance B\nM2 application" as B
control "B batch dispatcher" as W
database "Shared database\nqueue / execution authority" as D
== 1. Accept into separate response scopes ==
C -> A : Submit M1
A -> D : Accept M1 and claim execution
D --> A : Committed
A --> C : M1 receipt and output
C -> B : Future queue submission M2
B -> D : Short transaction: accept ordered M2
D --> B : Committed association
B --> C : M2 receipt; retain its own SSE
B -> W : Register pending M2, then recheck
== 2. Publish real predecessor completion ==
A -> D : Commit context, terminal, and release
D --> A : Committed
A --> C : M1 terminal; close M1 SSE
loop Bounded instance-level batches
  W -> D : Read predecessor and queue head
  D --> W : Committed state
end
== 3. Claim, restore, and run M2 ==
W -> B : Candidate eligible for recheck
B -> D : Short transaction: recheck and claim M2
D --> B : One winning execution identity
B -> D : Restore internal model context
D --> B : Recoverable M1 result
B -> B : Start M2 with its own credentials
B --> C : M2 output on M2 SSE
B -> D : Commit M2 real completion
B --> C : M2 terminal; close M2 SSE
legend bottom left
Target-only and disabled. Public queue fields and failure policy need a separate design.
M2 credentials stay only in B memory. Restore from internal context, never ListEvents.
No object or token relay. Lost owner / credentials require separate recovery.
Lease expiry does not prove remote side effects stopped.
endlegend
@enduml

@startuml target_follow_up_classes
skinparam backgroundColor white
' All types and relations below are target-only; names are not frozen.
' Source: pi-mono-java@dfb90cac4e233e09a0b8f047f7e9f4682f5ad238
' campusclaw/src/main/java/com/huawei/hicampus/claw/codingagent/runtimeapi/runtime/RuntimeSessionEngineRegistry.java
' Symbols: register, find, createHolder. Observed behavior: process-local execution objects.
' Design reason: application-level queue authority stays separate from runtime and request credentials.
title Future FollowUp - target-only responsibility boundaries
top to bottom direction
hide empty members
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam nodesep 25
skinparam ranksep 30
skinparam ArrowColor #475569
skinparam ClassBorderColor #64748B
skinparam ClassBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
skinparam stereotypeFontSize 10

package "Web / API" as WEB {
  class EventsController <<singleton, target-only>>
}
package "Application" as APP {
  class "EventSubmission\nService" as EventSubmissionService <<singleton, target-only>>
  class FollowUpQueueService <<singleton, target-only>>
  class FollowUpDispatcher <<singleton per instance, target-only>>
  class "PendingSubmission\nRegistry" as PendingSubmissionRegistry <<singleton per instance, target-only>>
  interface "FollowUpQueue\nRepository" as FollowUpQueueRepository <<target-only>>
  class PendingSubmission <<memory only, target-only>>
}
package "Persistence adapter" as PERSIST {
  class "MyBatisFollowUp\nQueueRepository" as MyBatisFollowUpQueueRepository <<singleton, target-only>>
  class "Shared database\nqueue / claim authority" as DB <<durable store>>
}
package "Runtime boundary" as CORE {
  interface "RuntimeExecution\nLauncher" as RuntimeExecutionLauncher <<target-only>>
  interface "SessionContext\nRestorer" as SessionContextRestorer <<target-only>>
  class SessionExecution <<per execution, target-only>>
  interface ExecutionIO <<runtime port, target-only>>
}
WEB -[hidden]down- APP
APP -[hidden]down- CORE
CORE -[hidden]down- PERSIST
EventsController --> EventSubmissionService
EventSubmissionService --> FollowUpQueueService : admit
EventSubmissionService --> PendingSubmissionRegistry : register
FollowUpDispatcher --> PendingSubmissionRegistry : bounded candidates
FollowUpDispatcher --> FollowUpQueueService : recheck and claim
FollowUpQueueService --> FollowUpQueueRepository : transaction
MyBatisFollowUpQueueRepository ..|> FollowUpQueueRepository
MyBatisFollowUpQueueRepository --> DB : Mapper / DTO
FollowUpDispatcher --> RuntimeExecutionLauncher : launch after claim
RuntimeExecutionLauncher --> SessionContextRestorer : restore context
SessionContextRestorer -[norank]-> DB : internal context
RuntimeExecutionLauncher ..> SessionExecution : creates
SessionExecution --> ExecutionIO
PendingSubmissionRegistry "1" *-- "0..bounded" PendingSubmission
PendingSubmission ..|> ExecutionIO
legend bottom left
Future target-only; disabled in the current product.
Recheck queue and execution state in the claim transaction; no network IO under DB locks.
Controller uses RequestVO / ResponseVO; persistence uses Mapper / DTO.
endlegend
@enduml

@startuml target_follow_up_local_lifecycle
skinparam backgroundColor white
' Target-only local lifecycle, no public queue API or durable credentials.
' Source: pi-mono-java@dfb90cac4e233e09a0b8f047f7e9f4682f5ad238
' campusclaw/src/main/java/com/huawei/hicampus/claw/codingagent/runtimeapi/runtime/RuntimeSessionEngineRegistry.java
' Observed behavior: registry holds local execution objects only.
' Design reason: bound pending capacity and keep request credentials out of persistence.
title Future FollowUp - local lifecycle, not enabled
top to bottom direction
hide empty members
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam nodesep 25
skinparam ranksep 30
skinparam ArrowColor #475569
skinparam ClassBorderColor #64748B
skinparam ClassBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
skinparam stereotypeFontSize 10

class "PendingSubmission\nRegistry" as PendingSubmissionRegistry <<singleton, target-only>>
class PendingSubmission <<pending / execution, target-only>>
class CredentialSnapshot <<memory only, target-only>>
class "BoundedResponse\nBuffer" as BoundedResponseBuffer <<HTTP response, target-only>>
interface "RuntimeExecution\nLauncher" as RuntimeExecutionLauncher <<target-only>>
class SessionExecution <<execution, target-only>>
interface ExecutionIO <<runtime port, target-only>>
PendingSubmissionRegistry "1" *-- "0..bounded" PendingSubmission
PendingSubmission "1" *-- "1" CredentialSnapshot
PendingSubmission "1" *-- "0..1" BoundedResponseBuffer
PendingSubmission ..|> ExecutionIO
RuntimeExecutionLauncher ..> SessionExecution : create after claim
SessionExecution --> ExecutionIO
note bottom of PendingSubmission
  Disconnect detaches output, not accepted work.
  Credentials are cleared at final cleanup.
  Process loss requires a separate authorization policy.
end note
@enduml
